plication-description\" class=\"inactive eael-tab-item-trigger eael-tab-nav-item\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-tab=\"1\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-controls=\"application-description-tab\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                            \n                            \n                            \n                                                            <span class=\"eael-tab-title title-after-icon\" >Application description<\/span>                                                    <\/li>\n                                            <li id=\"neascope-product-line\" class=\"inactive eael-tab-item-trigger eael-tab-nav-item\" aria-selected=\"false\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-controls=\"neascope-product-line-tab\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                            \n                            \n                            \n                                                            <span class=\"eael-tab-title title-after-icon\" >neaSCOPE product line<\/span>                                                    <\/li>\n                                    <\/ul>\n            <\/div>\n            \n            <div class=\"eael-tabs-content\">\n\t\t        \n                    <div id=\"application-description-tab\" class=\"clearfix eael-tab-content-item inactive\" data-title-link=\"application-description-tab\">\n\t\t\t\t        <p>Using <a href=\"https:\/\/www.neaspec.com\/products\/neaspec-microscopes\/\"><strong>microscopes of the neaSCOPE series<\/strong><\/a>, it is possible to observe details of <strong>the secondary structure of individual amyloid fibers<\/strong> with 10nm spatial resolution.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_10004\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-10004\" style=\"width: 800px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-10004 size-large\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/08d14462-1024x503.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"393\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/08d14462-1024x503.png 1024w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/08d14462-300x148.png 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/08d14462-768x378.png 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/08d14462.png 1082w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-10004\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Structure analysis of individual amyloid fibers: AFM image and reflectance measurement<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>Thanks to the measured nano-FTIR spectra, you can reliably distinguish \u03b2-amyloid fiber with a predominant \u03b2-sheet or \u03b1-helix with the help of a band characteristic of amide I. Monitoring the formation of \u03b2-sheets at the nanoscale is essential for research into diseases such as mad cow disease or Alzheimer&#8217;s disease, and also for the development of new drugs.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_10009\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-10009\" style=\"width: 550px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-10009\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/d2d48b2e-300x282.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"550\" height=\"518\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/d2d48b2e-300x282.png 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/d2d48b2e-768x723.png 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/d2d48b2e.png 833w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 550px) 100vw, 550px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-10009\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Study of secondary structure of proteins using amide band I<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>You can find out more about this and <a href=\"https:\/\/www.neaspec.com\/application\/e-book-nanoscale-analysis-of-inorganic-materials\/\">other applications here<\/a>.<\/p>\n                    <\/div>\n\t\t        \n                    <div id=\"neascope-product-line-tab\" class=\"clearfix eael-tab-content-item inactive\" data-title-l